    "examples": [
      {
        "question_text": "A factory investigates the quality of the $3200$ pens it produced on Monday. Every pen produced that day is inspected.\nIdentify the population and classify the collection as a census or a sample.",
        "solution_text": "Population: **all $3200$ pens produced by the factory on Monday**.\nThis is a **census** because every pen in that population is inspected."
      },
      {
        "question_text": "Scientists investigate the salt content of the water in a river. They collect $600$ mL of water from the river to analyse.\nIdentify the population and classify the collection as a census or a sample.",
        "solution_text": "Population: **all water in the river**.\nThis is a **sample** because the $600$ mL collected is only part of the river's water."
      },
      {
        "question_text": "Researchers investigate the travel habits of all adult residents of a city. They survey every adult resident of one apartment building, containing $120$ adults. Separately, they survey $640$ adults selected across the city. Neither collection includes every adult resident of the city.\nIdentify the population and classify each collection as a census or a sample.",
        "solution_text": "Population: **all adult residents of the city**.\nThe apartment-building collection is a **sample** because the building's $120$ adults are only part of the city's adult population.\nThe citywide collection is also a **sample** because it includes only $640$ adults, rather than every adult resident."
      },
      {
        "question_text": "An inspector investigates the quality of all pens produced by Factory A on Tuesday and all pens produced by Factory B on Tuesday.\nFactory A produced $2800$ pens, and $50$ are inspected. Factory B produced $1900$ pens, and every one is inspected.\nIdentify the population for each factory and classify each collection as a census or a sample.",
        "solution_text": "Factory A population: **all $2800$ pens produced by Factory A on Tuesday**.\nIts collection is a **sample** because only $50$ of those pens are inspected.\nFactory B population: **all $1900$ pens produced by Factory B on Tuesday**.\nIts collection is a **census** because every pen in that population is inspected."
      }
    ],
